<dispatchitem code="00007539.0001001" func-code="22-60-01" item-list-nbr="01" revdate="2021-05-19T00:00:00"><title><abb>FAC</abb> 1</title><ditembody nb-installed="1"><dispcond code="00007539.0001001.001" dispcond-id="D00858" dispcond-label="A" lid="N.00007539.0001001.001"><normal-dispcond nb-required="1" rectification-interval="-"><remark><requirement lid="N.00007539.0001001.002" req-id="R00859"><maintenance-ref><taskref chap-nbr="27" func="040" product="AMM Task" sect-nbr="22" seq="001" subj-nbr="00"/><taskref chap-nbr="27" func="040" product="AMM Task" sect-nbr="23" seq="001" subj-nbr="00"/></maintenance-ref><para code="00007539.0001001.005" layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.009">Must be operative.</para></requirement><note code="00007539.0001001.003" layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.003"><para layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.004">The <ecam-data ecamimportance="A" type="alert"><ecamsys>AUTO FLT</ecamsys><ecamtitle>FAC 1 FAULT</ecamtitle></ecam-data> alert may be displayed with the associated <tech-label type="cb">AUTO FLT/FAC1/28VDC</tech-label> tripped.</para><para layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.010">This may be due to
a short circuit within either rudder trim actuator channel 1 or rudder
travel limitation unit channel 1.</para><para layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.005">In this case, the <abb>FAC</abb> 1 may be recovered provided that the affected part of the
rudder system is deactivated using the associated maintenance procedure.</para><para layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.011">Refer to AMM 27-22-00-040-001,
or</para><para layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.012">Refer to AMM 27-23-00-040-001.</para><para layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.006"><duref product="MMEL" ref="00008324"/>, or </para><para layer="1" lid="N.00007539.0001001.007"><duref product="MMEL" ref="00008330"/></para></note></remark></normal-dispcond></dispcond></ditembody></dispatchitem>